<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="ecbf884">&lt;p&gt;
    A catalog of systems that the package will need to be integrated with in order to achieve the desired
    business functionality. It is an exhaustive list of the integrations that the business will need. Some of these
    integrations may be available out of the box (OOTB) within the package.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    The inventory should contain specific protocols and details on each integrations (e.g., in-bound versus out-bound). It
    can also help during root cause analysis on defects since integration information is stored in this single document.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="35806e0"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="9f0f4eb7"></attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="a1c6970e"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="f99ba4c5">&lt;p&gt;
    To list custom development elements required to address identified gaps in functionality where the standard
    package is unable to meet requirements.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
